{
  "id": "ac81871d-52e0-4c68-b39b-c8dbb67de52c",
  "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
  "data": {
    "body": "Consider the limit $\\lim_{(x,y)\\rightarrow(0,0)}\\frac{xy}{x^{2}+y^{2}}$. Which of the following statements is true?",
    "solution": [
      5
    ],
    "answerChoices": [
      {
        "id": "81057dbe-6317-4632-b5b7-78695614f73d",
        "index": 0,
        "body": "The limit does not exist, because the path-restricted limit approaching $(0,0)$ along the diagonal $y=x$ does not exist.",
        "questionId": "ac81871d-52e0-4c68-b39b-c8dbb67de52c",
        "stats": {
          "count": 100
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "c7b7f014-4ad5-4fa7-b7b8-f674d7fba93a",
        "index": 1,
        "body": "The limit is $0$, even though the path-restricted limits approaching $(0,0)$ along the $x$-axis and the $y$-axis are different.",
        "questionId": "ac81871d-52e0-4c68-b39b-c8dbb67de52c",
        "stats": {
          "count": 23
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "81ed1c11-9154-492c-9b08-165e6f7f656a",
        "index": 2,
        "body": "The limit is $0$, and the limit along any path approaching $(0,0)$ is also $0$.",
        "questionId": "ac81871d-52e0-4c68-b39b-c8dbb67de52c",
        "stats": {
          "count": 65
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "ba3ce34f-e55f-480e-b54d-9b12399c02f7",
        "index": 3,
        "body": "The limit does not exist, because the path-restricted limits approaching $(0,0)$ along the $x$-axis and the $y$-axis are different.",
        "questionId": "ac81871d-52e0-4c68-b39b-c8dbb67de52c",
        "stats": {
          "count": 124
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "ad7b893c-9216-4613-a8b9-8ba9ab24b8cb",
        "index": 4,
        "body": "The limit is $0$, because the path-restricted limit approaching $(0,0)$ along the diagonal $y=x$ is $0$.",
        "questionId": "ac81871d-52e0-4c68-b39b-c8dbb67de52c",
        "stats": {
          "count": 23
        },
        "resources": []
      },
      {
        "id": "bfc4bf58-bf5a-49c6-bccd-d233f148a334",
        "index": 5,
        "body": "The limit does not exist, even though the path-restricted limits approaching $(0,0)$ along the $x$-axis and the $y$-axis are both $0$.",
        "questionId": "ac81871d-52e0-4c68-b39b-c8dbb67de52c",
